{"article":{"id":213895229,"url":"https://bitfinex.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/213895229.json","html_url":"https://support.bitfinex.com/hc/en-us/articles/213895229-Margin-call-policy-on-Bitfinex","author_id":7843151305,"comments_disabled":true,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":7,"vote_sum":0,"vote_count":0,"section_id":900000103686,"created_at":"2016-12-08T12:41:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T12:38:59Z","name":"Margin call policy on Bitfinex","title":"Margin call policy on Bitfinex","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2026-01-17T16:54:26Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":1723454,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":["trading"],"body":"<h2 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\" id=\"h_01HVW85XC6EP0MAY3K1S2XHJFN\"><strong>What is a margin call</strong></h2><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A </span><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">margin call</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a notification that a position is in danger of liquidation. </span><br><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"></span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To avoid the liquidation of your position, you must maintain the minimum </span><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">maintenance margin</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. The </span><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">maintenance margin</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is the minimum net equity* required to keep the position open, and this is represented as a percentage of the value of your open positions. </span><br><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"></span></p><p><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">* Net Equity = Margin Wallet Balance + Adjusted P/L - Funding costs</span></em></p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Note</strong></span><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: Adjusted P/L represents a conservative valuation that includes 0.2% execution buffer. The actual realized P/L may differ depending on market conditions.</span></em></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You will receive a margin call (website and email notification when possible) when your net equity drops below 1.5x the maintenance margin of the value of your open positions. </span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For example, the maintenance margin for BTC/USD is currently 5% - when your net equity is worth 5% of the value of your open position. You will be margin called for your BTC/USD position at 7.5%.</span></em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> </span><br><strong>Note:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> When you have multiple positions open, the minimum maintenance margin is a weighted average of all positions.</span><br><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"></span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When the net value of your account equity falls below the required maintenance margin, your positions will be force-liquidated.</span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><strong>Important:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> In the case of a sudden and wide market movement, the email notification might </span><strong>not</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> be delivered quickly enough or not delivered at all if your account equity drops below 1.5x the maintenance margin. Market movement such as this could lead to the force-liquidation of your positions within seconds. During periods of high volatility, make sure to hold enough collateral to sustain your positions and monitor the website for further notifications. </span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The maintenance margin varies according to the trading pairs you open positions with. If you are trading pairs that Bitfinex considers higher risk, you may see your position liquidated at a higher maintenance margin. With an open margin position, you will see an estimated liquidation price (the price at which your position would be liquidated).</span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><strong>Note:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> The liquidation price displayed is only indicative and not a contractual price.</span></p><h2 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\" id=\"h_01HVW85XC76BFGE5A5VSJXCRY3\"><strong>What is the Required Equity</strong></h2><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For instance, if a margin position is worth $500 and a maintenance margin value of 15%, the Margin Wallet net equity must not fall below $75 to prevent a forced liquidation.</span></em></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When a position is force-liquidated, the system places a limit order at the zero-equity price or a market order for smaller positions.</span></p><h2 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\" id=\"h_01HVW85XC7S3HJBFYKYWAD0N9H\"><strong>Which currencies are considered high-risk on Bitfinex</strong></h2><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each trading pair has its own margin requirements. For certain pairs, the requirements are adjusted according to their current market risk.</span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can see the </span><em>Risk-Adjusted Initial Margin<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> &amp; </span>Risk-Adjusted Maintenance Margin</em> in the summary box<strong>, </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">representing the new requirements.</span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><strong>Important:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> This list of currencies considered to be risk currencies are subject to change.</span></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-justify\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you have any questions, please feel free to reach out to </span><a href=\"https://cs.bitfinex.com/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bitfinex Support</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. We are happy to assist you through this process!</span></p>","user_segment_ids":[]}}